    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af44d5a4_ddcae001",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/instance.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T10:14:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The nonce is only optional in the two `*_randnonce` APIs, while for all other AEAD algorithms[1], it is mandatory. In fact, both the nonce and the key are essential for ensuring the security of the AEAD algorithm. Users typically prefer to have control over the nonce or to use it to build a specific format, such as CoseEncrypt. Also the bssl team does recommend to use the two `*_randnonce` APIs.\n\nRegarding `ad`, since it serves to provide contextual info to the algorithm similar to the `info` field of HKDF, I just make them take the same type to keep the consistency.\n\n[1] https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/chromium-boringssl-docs/aead.h.html",
      "parentUuid": "55894b2f_5438fcdf",
